- No frontend tooling, framework version, or state-mgmt choice is recorded anywhere in the repo — this is a real open decision, not an oversight to route around.

ROUTES:
`/login` (public) → `/admin/{dashboard,questions,assignments,assignments/:id,students,students/:id,history}` (ROLE_ADMIN) and `/student/{dashboard,assignments,practice/:questionId?,history,wrong}` (ROLE_STUDENT). Question CRUD/GPT-generate stay as modals over `/admin/questions` rather than separate routes, matching the wireframe's modal UX.

COMPONENTS:
`app/` (routes + shell), `auth/` (AuthProvider, LoginPage, RequireRole guard), `api/` (fetch client with auth-header injection + 401→refresh→retry, per-domain call modules), `domains/questions/*` (ListPage, FilterBar, Table, DetailModal, CreateModal, GenerateModal, GeneratedQuestionReview — full breakdown in plan file), `domains/{dashboard,assignments,students,history,practice,wrongAnswers}` stubbed for later phases, `shared/ui` componentizing the wireframe's CSS primitives (Card, MetricCard, Btn variants, StatusBadge, ProgressBar, Modal, Toast, DataTable). Domain-first grouping mirrors the backend's own domain-first convention.

API_DEPENDENCIES:
Auth endpoints — implemented, safe to build against now. Question/Assignment/Student/StudyRecord/Dashboard/Me/WrongAnswer endpoints — documented only, not implemented; Question domain is the immediate blocker for the Phase 1 screen and is reportedly in progress on a peer session.

